===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[tempt]] with, to [[appeal]] or [[cater]] to ([[improper]] [[motivations]], etc.); to assist in gratification.
#: {{ux|en|His latest speech '''panders''' to the worst instincts of the electorate.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2020 July 29|author=Howard Johnston|title=Reversing Beeching: just how serious is the DfT?|journal=Rail|page=30|text=[...] both the Conservatives and Labour are guilty of '''pandering''' to the road lobby at the time of Beeching's ''The Reshaping of Britain's Railways'' report published in 1963.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To offer [[illicit]] sex with a third party; to [[pimp]].
# {{lb|en|transitive|obsolete}} To act as a pander for (somebody).

